WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.142
"Caveats and Side Effects
of Taurine Supplements"

00:00:07.268 --> 00:00:11.520
To taurine or not to taurine,
that's the question.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.800
Taurine is an ingredient
in some so-called energy drinks,

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.600
which some people consume
to improve physical performance,

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.800
although there is
little evidence

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.280
that taurine per se
exerts any beneficial effects

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.200
in healthy individuals,
or animals,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.200
without taurine depletion.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.080
But that was written
before this seminal study,

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.840
published in one
of our most prestigious

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.200
scientific journals,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.120
showing that
taurine supplementation

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.400
starting in middle-age

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.720
can significantly improve
the healthspan and lifespan

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.040
of a number
of different animals.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.920
Now, not all animal studies
have shown benefit.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.360
Lifelong
taurine supplementation

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.360
induced retardation
of learning

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.480
in mice, for example,

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.120
and low doses of taurine
significantly enhanced

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.960
lung tumor growth in mice,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.680
which led the authors to suggest
that lung cancer patients

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.640
may want to stay away
from drinks with taurine.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.800
You probably wouldn't want
to consume too much taurine

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.880
if you have
kidney failure either,

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.960
since taurine levels
are normally regulated

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.480
by our kidneys.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.960
The acute symptoms
of taurine overload,

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.000
mainly dizziness,

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.480
were relatively mild
and rapidly disappeared

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.200
after stopping taurine,
but researchers suggested

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.960
there should be
warning-type labels

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.480
on beverages containing taurine

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.160
to caution patients
with kidney failure

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.840
from drinking them.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.480
Similarly, patients
who have bleeding disorders

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.160
may not want to take taurine
since it might thin our blood.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.720
Psoriasis patients
may also want to steer clear,

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.400
as taurine evidently causes

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.040
a predictable,
intense itching response

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.200
that can last a day or two,
making skin lesions worse.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.640
It even caused the same reaction

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.800
in psoriasis patients
in remission.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.920
Pregnant and lactating women
are pretty much encouraged

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.760
to stay away
from any and all supplements

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.120
not specifically
prescribed for pregnancy.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.360
Similarly, individuals with
specific health conditions,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.040
such as bipolar disorder,

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.400
epilepsy,
or kidney problems,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.920
may want to be cautious.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.240
The only bipolar
problem I could find

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.160
were a few case reports
of mania blamed on Red Bull.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.440
This guy drank
20 cans of Red Bull,

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.600
that would make me manic too!

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.840
But, of course, Red Bull
has more than just taurine.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.920
Caffeine alone may do it.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.040
The epilepsy concern
may have to do with taurine

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.680
inhibiting detoxifying
enzymes in the liver

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.360
that are responsible
for breaking down

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.280
many commonly used drugs,
including anti-seizure drugs.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.680
It could also be
because of adverse reactions

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.680
reported by some patients
with epilepsy

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.840
who took 1.5 grams a day,

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.720
including nausea, headache,
dizziness, nose-bleed,

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.960
and mild walking disturbances,

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.520
but the epilepsy
seemed incidental.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.600
That may just be what sometimes
you see at higher doses.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.520
Potential side effects
of excessive consumption

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.680
of taurine supplements
beyond recommended doses

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.240
includes
gastrointestinal disturbances,

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.080
such as nausea,
vomiting, and diarrhea,

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.200
and neurological symptoms,

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.080
like dizziness,
tremors, and headaches.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.800
What are the recommended doses?

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.680
A proposed tolerated
upper safety limit

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.640
based on human clinical trials
is up to three grams a day,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.960
but the longest trial
at that dose

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.280
was only up to four months.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.080
In my last video,
I talked about a parallel

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.640
with another
conditionally non-essential

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.400
amino acid called arginine

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.520
that similarly looked good
in short-term trials,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.640
but by six months appeared
to be killing people,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.240
oopsie, so,
the study was shut down.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.880
So, who knows
if the supposed safe level

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.600
of three grams a day
is actually safe?

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.080
The dose used in
that promising animal study

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.440
might be equivalent
to dosing people

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.640
with even more than that,

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.760
and higher doses
aren't necessarily better.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.240
In this study on inflammation
and oxidative stress,

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.400
the lower doses,
three grams or less,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.640
appeared to work better.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.960
The thought is
that high doses of taurine

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:50.320
could downregulate
our own synthesis of taurine.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.680
Why would that be a problem?

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.280
Well, our body makes taurine

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.840
from another amino acid
called cysteine.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.320
So, if we're no longer
churning out taurine,

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.600
that may cause our levels
of cysteine to build up,

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.360
at least,
that's what happens in mice.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.640
And that might be bad

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.040
because chronically high
levels of cysteine

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.320
have been closely associated

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.080
with a whole list
of disease states

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.080
including rheumatoid arthritis,

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.720
Parkinson's, Alzheimer's,
lupus, cardiovascular disease,

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.960
and adverse pregnancy outcomes.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.120
On the other hand,
taurine may inhibit

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.040
our absorption
of another amino acid

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.000
called methionine,

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.360
since taurine and methionine

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.600
share the same
absorption transporter

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.760
through our intestinal lining.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.840
That would be presumed
to be a good thing,

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.680
since lowering methionine intake

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.760
is considered
a feasible strategy

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:36.240
against chronic
and aging-related diseases,

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.880
as I discussed
in How Not to Age.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.560
And, finally, the animal study

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.760
didn't address the impact of
taurine dietary supplementation

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:50.400
on the gut microbiome,
which I'll cover, next.

